WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.916
Hi, friends. This is the Listening Game.

00:00:12.916 --> 00:00:17.831
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.831 --> 00:00:20.781
Hands flat on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:20.781 --> 00:00:23.730
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:34.545
Listening is something your whole body does. Ears hear. Eyes watch the person talking. Hands stay quiet. Body stays still.

00:00:34.545 --> 00:00:45.359
Ears, eyes, quiet hands, still body — that is the listening body. Now the game: how much can you notice, just by listening?

00:00:45.359 --> 00:00:54.208
Round one: sounds. Eyes closed or soft. Listen for a sound that is far away…

00:00:54.208 --> 00:01:05.022
Now listen for a sound that is close by… Now the quietest sound in the room… Even quiet has a sound.

00:01:05.022 --> 00:01:17.803
Round two: listening for a word. I will say some words slowly. When you hear the word "calm," lift one finger — silently, so only you know.

00:01:17.803 --> 00:01:29.601
The breeze is soft… the river is calm… the garden is green… my breath is calm… the puppy is sleepy… the room is calm.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:35.499
If you lifted three fingers, you caught every "calm." Good listening.

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:45.331
Round three: partners. Turn in your chair to face your partner, the way your teacher showed you.

00:01:45.331 --> 00:01:53.196
Talkers: tell your partner about your favorite animal. Listeners: ears, eyes, quiet hands. Begin.

00:01:53.196 --> 00:02:09.196
…

00:02:09.196 --> 00:02:14.368
Listeners: tell your partner one thing you heard — out loud, just to them.

00:02:14.368 --> 00:02:18.801
Now switch. New talkers, new listeners. Begin.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:34.801
…

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:39.166
Good listening. Turn back around, hands flat on your desk.

00:02:39.166 --> 00:02:47.024
Ears, eyes, quiet hands — you listened with your whole body. That is the Listening Game.

00:02:47.024 --> 00:02:54.008
Listening is a kind of kindness. It tells a person: your words matter to me.

00:02:54.008 --> 00:02:56.627
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:56.627 --> 00:03:00.120
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.612
You're ready for what's next.
